Question 1: Spring Boot Data JPA – Product Inventory
Management System (@Version)
Scenario
Develop a Spring Boot application for a Product Inventory Management System. The
company wants to prevent multiple users from updating the same product record
simultaneously. Implement Optimistic Locking using the @Version annotation.
Requirements
Create an Entity named Product.
Field Type
productId Integer
productName String
price Double
quantity Integer
version Integer
Business Requirements
Create Product Entity.
Use @Version on the version field.
Create JPA Repository.
Save multiple product records.
Fetch a product using Product Id.
Update product details.
Verify that the version number automatically increments after every successful update.
Display all product details including version.
Concepts Covered
Spring Boot
Spring Data JPA
Entity Mapping
Repository
Optimistic Locking
